The n-th summand of the projection j_∞ is the Scott map from [D_∞ → D_∞] to D_∞ sending f to the level-(n+1) embedding of the conjugate j_{∞n} ∘ f ∘ i_{n∞}. It is conjugation by the pair (j_{∞n}, i_{n∞}), with values in D_{n+1}, followed by the embedding of level n+1. `jInfTerm.apply` says that this summand at a Scott map f equals that same level-(n+1) embedding of the conjugate. The two sides are definitionally equal.
